[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"231","stub":{"id":"231","section":"2. Park Boundary to Boyden Cave","altname":"","river":"Kings, S. Fork","difficulty":"IVtoVstandoutVplus","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"above-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"1500","dateTime":"2026-05-12T01:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108177","location":{"latitude":"36.8003","longitude":"-118.698"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"You can access the river at almost any location along this section, but this turn out works pretty well if you want to take out before the really big drops start.\n\nRun a last rapid to the left, past a huge boxy boulder.  Eddy out in the pool and take out behind the boulder.  A short trail leads up to the road.","id":"103042","location":{"latitude":"36.802799224853516","longitude":"-118.74800109863281"},"name":"Upper Take Out","distance":"3.2","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":true},{"type":"hazard","description":"As you drive upstream from Boyden Cave, you will see class 3 and 4 whitewater till you see the Last Cascade.  The change in difficulty will by obvious.  If you are looking for the Big Stuff, you have arrived.  Keep driving and enjoy. if you are looking for class 4 whitewater, turn around and park just below the cascade.  You will have to hunt around a bit to figure out the easiest launching spot.","id":"103043","location":{"latitude":"36.812652587890625","longitude":"-118.80794525146484"},"name":"Put in below Last Cascade","distance":"6.8","photoID":"0","difficulty":"V","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"113420","location":{"latitude":"36.8174","longitude":"-118.822"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"879610","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"","caption":"Close up of a Rapid","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879610","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879610"}},{"id":"879613","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"This drop is near the beginning of a long rapid immediately upstream of Grizzly Falls Picnic area.  ","caption":"Ledge drop","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879613","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879613"}},{"id":"879606","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"Looking downstream into the Horseshoe Bend section from the roadside section take out below Boyden Cave.   .  ","caption":"Take out view","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879606","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879606"}},{"id":"879611","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"One of about 4 class 4 rapids above Grizzly Falls Picnic Area.  ","caption":"Another 4","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879611","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879611"}},{"id":"879617","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"The run out below one of the huge drops.","caption":"Another Cascade","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879617","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879617"}},{"id":"879614","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"Part of the long rapid immediately upstream of Grizzly Falls Picnic area.  ","caption":"Ledge drop continued","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879614","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879614"}},{"id":"879616","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"Just some rapid in between the huge drops.","caption":"In between rapids","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879616","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879616"}},{"id":"879618","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"Some big drop that probably has mank above or below it.  I have forgotten already.  ","caption":"Picturesque Drop","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879618","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879618"}},{"id":"879619","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"The entry looks tricky, but what a beautiful drop! ","caption":"Is there a good line?","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879619","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879619"}},{"id":"879621","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"In between the huge drops can be some fairly long sections of excellent, continuous class 4, \"Boogy Water\".","caption":"Boogy Water 2","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879621","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879621"}},{"id":"879608","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"This good rapid is right below the bridge at Boyden Cave.  A small cave opening is visible in the background.   The rock is marble.","caption":"Marble Rapid","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879608","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879608"}},{"id":"879609","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"I think this is one of the busier rapids upstream of Grizzly Falls picnic area.","caption":"Busy Rapid","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879609","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879609"}},{"id":"16185","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2798","description":"One of many technical drops at this low flow.  ","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"Trevor Haagenson","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16185","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16185"}},{"id":"879622","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"This nice slalom runs past the Boyden Cave parking lot.  The cave employees reported that the largest boulder on the right in the photo was a few feet underwater during the peak spring flows.  ","caption":"Boyden Cave Rapid","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879622","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879622"}},{"id":"16186","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2798","description":"A fairly typical downstream view for much of the section from the park boundary to Grizzley Falls...","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"Trevor Haagenson","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16186","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16186"}},{"id":"879620","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"In between the huge drops can be some fairly long sections of excellent, continuous class 4, \"Boogy Water\".","caption":"Boogy Water","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879620","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879620"}},{"id":"879607","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"Looking upstream from the roadside section take out below Boyden Cave.   The big cliff is one side of \"The Gates of the Kings\".   The river has cut down through a ridge of marble, leaving impressive cliffs on both sides.","caption":"Gate of the Kings","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879607","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879607"}},{"id":"879612","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"This gauge is on the upstream side of the highway bridge just inside the park boundary.    This level is about 700 to 750 cfs.  ","caption":"Painted Gauge","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879612","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879612"}},{"id":"879615","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880195","description":"This cascade is a couple of rapids downstream of Grizzly Falls Picnic area.  It is rather obvious from the road.  It is the first of the really big drops.  I watched Phil Martin run it once.","caption":"Phil's cascade","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879615","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879615"}},{"id":"16184","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2799","description":"Trevor loosens up at the put-in pool at the Kings Canyon Nat. Park boundary.   The first rapid is a long class 4ish technical slalom.  ","caption":"Park Boundary Put-in","poi_name":"","subject":"Trevor Haagensen","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16184","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16184"}}],"detail":{"id":"231","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The South Fork Kings is very pretty and worth visiting just for the spectacular scenery.   The whitewater is also excellent with two sections of class 4 boating, seperated by a section of class 5, 5+ and class 6 intermixed with great looking class 4. The river is all roadside so it is easy to pick and choose what you feel like boating.   Flows on this section drop into runnable range after many other rivers have dried up, so it is an excellent late season destination.\n\nDirections: From Fresno, take highway 180 through Grant's Grove towards Cedar Grove. Highway 180 climbs over Cherry Gap (6800 feet) then drops down into Kings Canyon. The road finally reaches the river at Boyden Cave, then follows the river to Cedar Grove.\n\nBoating is not allowed on the SF Kings inside Kings Canyon Nat. Park from the confluence with Bubbs Creek to the park boundary.   See: [Seki boating.](http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/rivers.htm)   The river through Cedar Grove is mostly class 1 & 2 and would attract the unskilled.  There is at least one short section of class 5 and perhaps a section or two of class 4 or class 3.\n\nThere are two sections of moderate whitewater between the Park boundary and Boyden Cave, seperated by a long section of very big drops and monstrous cascades.\n\nThe lower moderate section is about 1 mile long and ends at or just downstream of Boyden Cave. It is class 4 at reasonable flows but quite continuous. Put-in below the obvious monster rapids.\n\nThere is also a 3 mile moderate section from the park boundary to the Grizzley Falls picnic area. (Grizzley Falls is on a side creek) Depending on flow, the bigger rapids in this section are class 4 to class 5.\n\nPut-in: Drive along the river till you see the park boundary sign. Park next to it but downhill and carry boats through the woods to the river. The Park boundary rapid is a wonderful, long, steep slalom, so it is nice to boat all of it.\n\nTake-out below Grizzley Creek where the river comes back to the road, but upstream of a big cascade.\n\nMuch of the difficult section between Grizzley Creek and Boyden has been boated at one time or another, and there are many very interesting drops. However, there are many really ugly (from a boating perspective) cascades throughout the section. If you like to run one monster drop after another, but with easy roadside scouting, this could be your place.\n\nPaul Martzen\n\nA GUIDE TO THE BEST WHITEWATER IN THE STATE OF CA, HOLBEK & STANLEY, 1988","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"8","correlations":[{"reachID":"231","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"200","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"SF KINGS R ABV ROARING R","gaugeSource":"CDEC","gaugeSourceIdenti